findings.body:
**Concern.** `withMergeLock` runs the whole section, including `appendEvent(db, session.id, 'pr_closed', …)`, and only then checks the lock. If the lock was gone or replaced at release, it throws `MergeLockLostError` carrying the section's result ([merge-gate.service.ts](https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/bf7cb4b8131aad22264485c43e5b1739f39a790b/src/core/merge-gate.service.ts#L1286-L1294)). Decision 88 and the error's JSDoc require the caller to report that result before it fails: "Carries what the section returned, which happened all the same, for the caller to report before it fails". The new branch sends every non-interrupt error straight to `refuseScrubbed`:

```ts
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof GateInterruptedError) throw error;
  return refuseScrubbed(error);
}
```

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/bf7cb4b8131aad22264485c43e5b1739f39a790b/src/cli/index.ts#L2633-L2638

**Trigger.** The lock directory is moved or replaced while the section runs. The section includes a `gh` call between the re-check and the write. The operator then sees only "The merge lock ... was gone or replaced". Every other refusal from `abandonClosedSession` means nothing was recorded, so the operator reads this one the same way. In fact the close was recorded and the ADR numbers were freed.

The sibling `pup land` (L2667-2674, L2698) and `pup retire` paths both catch `MergeLockLostError`, print the outcome, and only then call `refuseScrubbed(lockLost)`.

findings.suggestion:
let abandoned: { prUrl: string; recorded: boolean };
let lockLost: MergeLockLostError | undefined;
try {
  abandoned = await abandonClosedSession(db, { repoPath, sessionId: session, wait: true });
} catch (error) {
  if (error instanceof GateInterruptedError) throw error;
  if (!(error instanceof MergeLockLostError)) return refuseScrubbed(error);
  abandoned = error.result as { prUrl: string; recorded: boolean };
  lockLost = error;
}
console.log(
  abandoned.recorded
    ? `Recorded ${abandoned.prUrl} as closed unmerged: the ADR-number check no longer ` +
        `counts ${sanitizeReason(session)}'s decisions.`
    : `${abandoned.prUrl} was already recorded as closed unmerged.`,
);
if (lockLost !== undefined) refuseScrubbed(lockLost);
return;
